<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Projects | MySite</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>
  <nav class="navbar">
    <h2>MySite</h2>
    <div>
      <a href="index.html">Home</a>
      <a href="about.html">About</a>
      <a href="projects.html">Projects</a>
      <a href="contact.html">Contact</a>
      <button onclick="toggleDarkMode()">Dark Mode</button>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section class="page">
    <h1>Projects</h1>
    <p>Selected projects built with Python, data analysis, quantitative research, and AI-assisted workflows.</p>

    <div class="project-toolbar">
      <input
        id="projectSearch"
        type="text"
        placeholder="Search projects..."
        oninput="filterProjects()"
      >

      <select id="projectFilter" onchange="filterProjects()">
        <option value="all">All Projects</option>
        <option value="quant">Quant</option>
        <option value="python">Python</option>
        <option value="data">Data Analysis</option>
        <option value="ai">AI-Assisted</option>
      </select>

      <button onclick="resetProjectFilters()">Reset</button>
      <span id="projectCount"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="project-grid">

      <div class="project-card" data-tags="python data ai quant factor a-share">
        <h2>AI-Assisted A-Share Single Factor Analysis</h2>

        <p class="project-subtitle">
          A quantitative research workflow for analyzing single-factor effectiveness in the A-share market.
        </p>

        <img
          src="images/single-factor-analysis.png"
          alt="JupyterLab screenshot of single factor analysis project"
          class="project-image"
        >

        <div class="project-content">
          <h3>Project Overview</h3>
          <p>
            This project uses Python and Jupyter Notebook to build a single-factor analysis workflow
            for the SSE 50 stock universe. It focuses on factor cleaning, return alignment,
            industry data processing, IC analysis, grouped return testing, and visualization.
          </p>

          <button class="small-button" onclick="toggleDetails('factor-details')">
            Show / Hide Details
          </button>

          <div id="factor-details" class="project-details">
            <h3>Core Pain Point</h3>
            <p>
              Traditional factor research often requires repeated data cleaning, manual field matching,
              and fragmented backtesting code. This project creates a reusable research template for
              testing and validating factor signals.
            </p>

            <h3>AI / Agent Usage</h3>
            <p>
              AI was used as a coding and research assistant for project structure design, code generation,
              debugging, data-processing logic, and error diagnosis.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
          <div class="tags">
            <span>Python</span>
            <span>pandas</span>
            <span>NumPy</span>
            <span>matplotlib</span>
            <span>scikit-learn</span>
            <span>statsmodels</span>
            <span>Jupyter Notebook</span>
          </div>

          <div class="project-links">
            <a href="files/Single_Factor_Analysis.html" target="_blank">View Results Report</a>
            <a href="files/Single_Factor_Analysis.ipynb" target="_blank">View Notebook</a>
            <a href="files/Single_Factor_Analysis.py" target="_blank">View Python Script</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-card" data-tags="python data quant backtesting yfinance trading">
        <h2>Quant Moving Average Crossover Backtest</h2>

        <p class="project-subtitle">
          A Python-based quantitative trading backtest using a moving average crossover strategy.
        </p>

        <img
          src="projects/quant-ma-crossover/results/equity_curve.png"
          alt="Equity curve for moving average crossover backtest"
          class="project-image"
        >

        <div class="project-content">
          <h3>Project Overview</h3>
          <p>
            This project downloads historical SPY price data, generates trading signals,
            applies transaction costs, calculates performance metrics, and exports both
            CSV results and an equity curve chart.
          </p>

          <button class="small-button" onclick="toggleDetails('quant-details')">
            Show / Hide Details
          </button>

          <div id="quant-details" class="project-details">
            <h3>Strategy Logic</h3>
            <p>
              The strategy buys when the short moving average is above the long moving average,
              and stays in cash when the short moving average falls below the long moving average.
              The current test uses a 20-day and 50-day moving average pair.
            </p>

            <h3>Backtest Results</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Total Return: 104.40%</li>
              <li>Annual Return: 7.58%</li>
              <li>Annual Volatility: 11.43%</li>
              <li>Sharpe Ratio: 0.66</li>
              <li>Max Drawdown: -29.60%</li>
              <li>Number of Trades: 47</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <h3>Tech Stack</h3>
          <div class="tags">
            <span>Python</span>
            <span>pandas</span>
            <span>NumPy</span>
            <span>matplotlib</span>
            <span>yfinance</span>
            <span>Backtesting</span>
          </div>

          <div class="project-links">
            <a href="quant-project.html">View Project Page</a>
            <a href="projects/quant-ma-crossover/README.md" target="_blank">README</a>
            <a href="projects/quant-ma-crossover/main.py" target="_blank">Python Code</a>
            <a href="projects/quant-ma-crossover/results/backtest_results.csv" target="_blank">CSV Results</a>
            <a href="projects/quant-ma-crossover/results/equity_curve.png" target="_blank">Equity Curve</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <button id="backToTop" onclick="scrollToTop()">Top</button>

  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
